===== Specific Configuration =====

<WRAP BOX>

==== Network interfaces ====
The default network configuration is:
^ Interface Name   ^ Description          ^ Default configuration    ^
| br-lan           | LAN & WiFi           | 192.168.1.1/24   |
| eth0             | WAN, LAN ports (1 to 4)   | None             |
| eth0.1           | LAN ports (1 to 4)   | DHCP             |
| eth0.2           | WAN port             | DHCP             |
| phy0-ap0         | WiFi                 | Disabled         |

</WRAP>

==== Switch Ports ====
<WRAP BOX>

^ Port             ^ Switch port   ^
| Internet (WAN)   | 0     |
| LAN 1            | 1     |
| LAN 2            | 2     |
| LAN 3            | 3     |
| LAN 4            | 4     |

</WRAP>

==== Buttons ====
-> [[docs:guide-user:hardware:hardware.button]] on howto use and configure the hardware button(s).
Here, we merely name the buttons, so we can use them in the above Howto.

<WRAP BOX>

The SNR CPE-W4N has the following buttons:

^ BUTTON             ^ Event   ^ Pin ^ Active ^
| RST                |  reset  | GPIO#1   | High |

</WRAP>

==== LEDs ====

<WRAP BOX>

The SNR CPE-W4N has the following LEDs:

^ BUTTON             ^ Event   ^ Pin ^ Active ^
| SYS                |  failsafe, upgrade  | GPIO#38   | Low |
| WPS                |  running  | GPIO#39   | High |
| WLAN                |  wlan  | GPIO#72   | Low |

</WRAP>

